{"id":"ae87aaa90aca","path":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/career-prospects","lang":"en","title":"Employability","description":"Great career prospects ahead! Discover what happens after the Master in Digital Fashion Communication and the opportunies that are waiting for you.","section":"Education","crumbs":["Education","Master","MDFC","Career Prospects"],"image":null,"words":177,"alternates":{"en":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/career-prospects"},"breadcrumb":[{"label":"Home","path":"/en"},{"label":"Education","path":"/en/originalnode/8525"},{"label":"Master","path":"/en/originalnode/7757"},{"label":"MDFC","path":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication"},{"label":"Career Prospects","path":null},{"label":"Employability","path":null}],"blocks":[{"t":"html","html":"<p>Professional opportunities for graduates are related to <strong>communication management </strong>and <strong>strategy </strong>for the fashion industry in any type of company, from small start-ups to large international corporations. Graduates are prepared to work in functions like digital and social media marketing, brand development, data and e-Commerce management, advertising and PR, and CSR coordination.</p> <p>Even if the master focuses on fashion communication, graduates might work in related experience-economy industries, e.g. arts, cultural heritage, tourism, luxury.</p><p>The following data are based on the last USI Alumni Survey, carried out by the USI Career&amp;Alumni Service and the USI Alumni DB. </p> <table> <tbody> <tr> <td> </td> <td> <p><strong>1 year after graduation</strong></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Employed</strong></p> </td> <td> <p>100%</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Time to job</strong></p> </td> <td> <p>-1 months</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Salary</strong><br> Average/100% gross annual salary in CH</p> </td> <td> <p>CHF 70'000.-</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Place of work</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>%</strong></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Switzerland</p> <ul> <li>Ticino</li> <li>Other Swiss Cantons</li> </ul> </td> <td> <p>38.1</p> <ul> <li>26.2</li> <li>11.9</li> </ul> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Italy</p> </td> <td> <p>32.1</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Other Countries</p> </td> <td> <p>29.8</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Industries (main)</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>%</strong></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Luxury goods and Fashion</p> </td> <td> <p>51.6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Communication, PR, and Marketing</p> </td> <td> <p>17.6</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Informatics, Technology, Web</p> </td> <td> <p>5.5</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Media</p> </td> <td> <p>4.4</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> </td> <td> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p><strong>Main Employment Functions</strong></p> </td> <td> <p><strong>%</strong></p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>Communication, PR</p> </td> <td> <p>35.3</p> </td> </tr> <tr> <td>Marketing and events</td> <td>32.9</td> </tr> <tr> <td> <p>E-commerce, Digital</p> </td> <td> <p>10.6</p> </td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Source: 2024 USI Master Survey (alumni 2023) and USI Alumni DB</p>"}],"ctas":[{"label":"Apply Now","href":"/en/education-application"}],"nav":[{"label":"Overview","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication"},{"label":"Partners","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/partners"},{"label":"Key facts","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/key-facts"},{"label":"Why this Master","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/why-this-master"},{"label":"Digital Fashion Communication","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/what-is-digital-fashion-communication"},{"label":"What is a Double Degree?","href":"/en/education/master/digital-fashion-communication/double-degree"},{"label":"Study plan","href":"/en/education/master/international-tourism/structure-and-